      <p class="eyebrow hero__eyebrow">Persuasion Literacy &middot; Marketing Psychology &middot; Clear Thinking</p>
      <h1 class="hero__headline">
        <span class="hero__line">You Were Handed</span>
        <span class="hero__line">a Script. Nobody</span>
        <span class="hero__line">Mentioned You</span>
        <span class="hero__line hero__line--italic"><em><span class="hero__drawn">Could Put It Down.</span></em></span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero__lede">You bought the thing. You used your real judgment, and it still worked on you. That isn't a character flaw. It's a design outcome. Brooke Reports takes apart the mechanisms that produce it, so you can see the next one while it's still running.</p>
      <p class="hero__small-line">Cozy detective agency energy, minus the murders. Investigating confusing sales pages, attention traps, internet hype, and suspiciously shiny promises.</p>
